1
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:17,250
Heroes so small they have to be seen on the big screen.

2
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:28,500
The Meerkats is a documentary, tv movie, family
film directed by James Honeyborne.

3
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:39,750
A coming of age story following a young meerkat pup, Kolo, growing up in the Kalahari desert; and an inspiring look at how one
family's connection to each other and their surroundings is a model of resilience and fortitude for us all.

4
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Shot using ground-breaking techniques, this dramatised documentary is a one-of-a-kind
presentation from The Weinstein Company and the BBC, featuring narration by Paul Newman.

5
00:25:56,250 --> 00:26:02,250
Narrator (voice), played by Paul Newman.

6
00:31:07,500 --> 00:31:13,500
Narrator (Russian release) (voice), played by Rufus Beck.

7
00:36:18,750 --> 00:36:24,750
Le narrateur (voix française), played by Guillaume Canet.

8
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
The Meerkats, also known as Meerkats: The Movie, is a feature-length 2008 British wildlife fiction film
which anthropomorphises the daily struggles of a clan of meerkats in the Kalahari Desert.

9
00:46:41,250 --> 00:46:47,250
It was produced by BBC Films, and filmed by the
award-winning BBC Natural History Unit.

10
00:51:52,500 --> 00:51:58,500
It is the debut directorial feature of James Honeyborne, previously a
producer of natural history programmes for television.

11
00:57:03,750 --> 00:57:09,750
The worldwide premiere was held at the Dinard Film Festival, France in
October 2008, expanding to a wide release the following week.

12
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:21,000
The film was released in 2009, on 7 August in the UK.

13
01:07:26,250 --> 01:07:32,250
The film was dedicated to Paul Newman, the narrator of the film, who died in 2008,
shortly before this film was released making it his final film role.

14
01:12:37,500 --> 01:12:43,500
The film explores themes of meerkat, kalahari desert,
animal life, animal behaviour, documentary.

15
01:17:48,750 --> 01:17:54,750
The tone is uplifting.
